The 2D transpose path of the copy kernel (lab proposal)

ggml_cont(ggml_transpose(x)) of a contiguous x gives a source whose row stride is one element.
The reshape path of cpy-ops.c then finds rows_contig false and copies one element for each
iteration of its loop. The gated delta net asks for that shape twice per layer
(src/models/delta-net-base.cpp:89 for the cumsum input, :123 and :124 for kb and kq of the
chunked path), thus every prefill pays it.

This proposal stages a 32 x 32 tile in the VTCM and transposes it with 32 independent gathers.
Measured in tools/htp-lab (target move, a 256 x 256 f32 transpose), both results byte for byte
equal to the reference: 3.02 cycles per element before, 0.51 after, thus 5.98 times faster.

The gather is cheap only when its result is not read by the next instruction. One gather with a
dependent load costs 45 cycles; 32 independent gathers cost 4.7 cycles each, because the unit
pipelines them. concat-ops.c already uses that pattern.

The stride of the source rows

The source of this path is the transposed view: nb00 of the view is one row of x, and nb01 is one
element (exec_cpy selects the path only for nb01 == 4). The kernel reads the 32 rows of each source
tile at the stride nb00 / 4, one row of x. A read at the stride nb01 / 4 = 1 float gives each
output row c the values x[c] thru x[c + 31] of one row of x, and not a column of x.

The kernel lab (tools/htp-lab, target v81move, the release flags, v79na_1 and v81na_2): the CONT of
a transposed 64 x 96 f32 matrix gives 0 of 6144 values that differ from the source with the stride
nb00 / 4, and 6048 with the stride of one float. The other cases of the target (CPY to f16,
SET_ROWS, GET_ROWS, ROPE, SOFT_MAX, GELU) give the same hashes with the two forms, and on the two
cores.

No graph of Qwen3.5 or of its vision encoder sends this shape: the delta net runs as the fused
GATED_DELTA_NET op, and the vision encoder uses ggml_cont_3d. The CONT cases of test-backend-ops
get four transposed matrices with two sides that are multiples of 32 (64 x 96, 256 x 256 x 2,
32 x 32 x 3 x 2 and 1024 x 64).

The phone stage v81 (the OnePlus 13, v79): test-backend-ops CPY, SET_ROWS, GET_ROWS and CONT on
HTP0 pass 293 of 293, with the four cases. llama-bench of the 4B Q8_0, this kernel against the
kernel with the stride of one float, 3 alternated rounds: pp512 1003.8 against 1012.0 t/s (the
standard deviation of one run is 14 to 22 t/s), tg32 at d0 10.69 against 10.63 t/s, tg32 at d4096
10.28 against 10.28 t/s.

